  "chapter": {
    "number": 90,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "hebrew_subtitle",
        "content": [
          "(91) Praise of a Song, by David."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 1,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "He that dwells in the help of the Highest, shall sojourn under the shelter of the God of heaven.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 2,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "He shall say to the Lord, You are my helper and my refuge: my God; I will hope in him.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 3,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For he shall deliver you from the snare of the hunters, from every troublesome matter.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 4,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "He shall overshadow you with his shoulders, and you shall trust under his wings: his truth shall cover you with a shield.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 5,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "You shall not be afraid of terror by night; nor of the arrow flying by day;",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 6,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "nor of the evil",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 175
          },
          {
            "text": "thing that walks in darkness; nor of calamity, and the evil spirit at noon-day.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 7,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "A thousand shall fall at your side, and ten thousand at your right hand; but it shall not come near you.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 8,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Only with your eyes shall you observe and see the reward of sinners.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 9,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For you, O Lord, are my hope: you, my soul, have made the Most High your refuge.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 10,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "No evils shall come upon you, and no scourge shall draw near to your dwelling.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 11,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For he shall give his angels charge concerning you, to keep you in all your ways.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 12,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "They shall bear you up on their hands, lest at any time you dash your foot against a stone.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 13,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "You shall tread on the asp and basilisk: and you shall trample on the lion and dragon.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 14,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For he has hoped in me, and I will deliver him: I will protect him, because he has known my name.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 15,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "He shall call upon me, and I will listen to him: I am with him in affliction; and I will deliver him, and glorify him.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 16,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "I will satisfy him with length of days, and show him my salvation.",
            "poem": 1
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "footnotes": [
      {
        "noteId": 175,
        "caller": "+",
        "text": "See ver 3.",
        "reference": {
          "chapter": 90,
          "verse": 6
        }
      }
    ]
